---
description: >-
  Every kanban label kind (column title, card text and a card in a quoted
  string) written the six ways of spec #1368: plain markdown, a quoted
  markdown string, bare backticks, a code span in plain text, the common
  tags and a written \n. Only the quoted markdown string reads markdown;
  the bare backticks and the code span are drawn as written, the tags draw
  and \n breaks the line.
---
kanban
  c1[column **bold** _ital_]
    k1[card **bold** _ital_]
    q1["quoted card **bold** _ital_"]
  c2["`column **bold** _ital_`"]
    k2["`card **bold** _ital_`"]
  c3[`column **bold** _ital_`]
    k3[`card **bold** _ital_`]
  c4[column a `code` b]
    k4[card a `code` b]
    q4["quoted card a `code` b"]
  c5[column <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O]
    k5[card <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O]
    q5["quoted card <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O"]
  c6[column one\ntwo]
    k6[card one\ntwo]
    q6["quoted card one\ntwo"]
